{
  "id": "32176d90-941b-545c-8252-ad4084b07275",
  "quality_score": 0.92,
  "review_status": "auto-approved",
  "content_json": {
    "id": "tr-a2-past-copula",
    "cefr": "A2",
    "title": "Past & evidential copula on nominals",
    "sections": [
      {
        "id": "what-is-it",
        "body": [
          {
            "kind": "paragraph",
            "text": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "text": "Turkish has no standalone verb meaning «to be» in the present tense — the copula is a suffix. In the past, however, it surfaces as a distinct suffix attached directly to a nominal predicate (a noun, adjective, or adverbial). There are two past copulas: "
              },
              {
                "kind": "hilite",
                "children": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "text": "-(y)DI"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "text": ", which marks a past state the speaker witnessed or knows directly (e.g. "
              },
              {
                "kind": "em",
                "children": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "text": "hastaydım"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "text": " — «I was ill»), and "
              },
              {
                "kind": "hilite",
                "children": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "text": "-(y)mIş"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "text": ", which marks a past state reported second-hand or inferred (e.g. "
              },
              {
                "kind": "em",
                "children": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "text": "hastaymış"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "text": " — «she was apparently ill»). Both suffixes carry their own set of personal endings and follow standard four-way vowel harmony. They are not the same as the verbal past tense suffix "
              },
              {
                "kind": "strong",
                "children": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "text": "-DI"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "text": " added to verb stems."
              }
            ]
          }
        ],
        "title": "what is it?"
      },
      {
        "id": "when-to-use-it",
        "body": [
          {
            "kind": "list",
            "items": [
              [
                {
                  "kind": "paragraph",
                  "text": [
                    {
                      "kind": "strong",
                      "children": [
                        {
                          "kind": "text",
                          "text": "Direct past states with -(y)DI."
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "kind": "text",
                      "text": " Use this when you personally witnessed or experienced the state: a past identity, quality, location, or condition. The speaker has first-hand knowledge."
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ],
              [
                {
                  "kind": "paragraph",
                  "text": [
                    {
                      "kind": "strong",
                      "children": [
                        {
                          "kind": "text",
                          "text": "Past existence with vardı / yoktu."
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "kind": "text",
                      "text": " The existence words "
                    },
                    {
                      "kind": "em",
                      "children": [
                        {
                          "kind": "text",
                          "text": "var"
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "kind": "text",
                      "text": " («there is») and "
                    },
                    {
                      "kind": "em",
                      "children": [
                        {
                          "kind": "text",
                          "text": "yok"
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "kind": "text",
                      "text": " («there is not») take the same -(y)DI suffix to give "
                    },
                    {
                      "kind": "hilite",
                      "children": [
                        {
                          "kind": "text",
                          "text": "vardı"
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "kind": "text",
                      "text": " («there was») and "
                    },
                    {
                      "kind": "hilite",
                      "children": [
                        {
                          "kind": "text",
                          "text": "yoktu"
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "kind": "text",
                      "text": " («there was not»). These are fixed third-person forms and do not change for person."
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ],
              [
                {
                  "kind": "paragraph",
                  "text": [
                    {
                      "kind": "strong",
                      "children": [
                        {
                          "kind": "text",
                          "text": "Reported or inferred past states with -(y)mIş."
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "kind": "text",
                      "text": " Use this when you did not witness the state yourself — you heard it from someone else, read it, or are inferring it from evidence. It is often translated as «apparently», «reportedly», or «I hear that»."
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            ]
          }
        ],
        "title": "when to use it?"
      },
      {
        "id": "formation",
        "body": [
          {
            "kind": "paragraph",
            "text": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "text": "Both suffixes attach to the predicate and then take personal endings. The key rule: if the predicate ends in a "
              },
              {
                "kind": "strong",
                "children": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "text": "vowel"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "text": ", insert a buffer "
              },
              {
                "kind": "hilite",
                "children": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "text": "-y-"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "text": " before the suffix. If it ends in a "
              },
              {
                "kind": "strong",
                "children": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "text": "consonant"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "text": ", attach directly. The vowel in both suffixes follows four-way harmony (I = ı / i / u / ü)."
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "kind": "paragraph",
            "text": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "text": "-(y)DI takes "
              },
              {
                "kind": "strong",
                "children": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "text": "Group 1"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "text": " personal endings (the same set used with the verbal -DI past): -m, -n, -(zero), -k, -nIz, -lAr."
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "head": [
              "person",
              "stem + suffix",
              "meaning"
            ],
            "kind": "conjugation-table",
            "rows": [
              [
                "ben",
                "hasta-y-dı-m",
                "I was ill"
              ],
              [
                "sen",
                "hasta-y-dı-n",
                "you were ill"
              ],
              [
                "o",
                "hasta-y-dı",
                "he/she/it was ill"
              ],
              [
                "biz",
                "hasta-y-dı-k",
                "we were ill"
              ],
              [
                "siz",
                "hasta-y-dı-nız",
                "you (pl.) were ill"
              ],
              [
                "onlar",
                "hasta-y-dı-lar",
                "they were ill"
              ]
            ]
          },
          {
            "kind": "callout",
            "variant": "default",
            "children": [
              {
                "kind": "paragraph",
                "text": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "text": "Consonant-final stem example: "
                  },
                  {
                    "kind": "em",
                    "children": [
                      {
                        "kind": "text",
                        "text": "öğrenci"
                      }
                    ]
                  },
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "text": " ends in a vowel → "
                  },
                  {
                    "kind": "hilite",
                    "children": [
                      {
                        "kind": "text",
                        "text": "öğrenciydim"
                      }
                    ]
                  },
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "text": ". "
                  },
                  {
                    "kind": "em",
                    "children": [
                      {
                        "kind": "text",
                        "text": "evde"
                      }
                    ]
                  },
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "text": " ends in a vowel → "
                  },
                  {
                    "kind": "hilite",
                    "children": [
                      {
                        "kind": "text",
                        "text": "evdeydim"
                      }
                    ]
                  },
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "text": ". "
                  },
                  {
                    "kind": "em",
                    "children": [
                      {
                        "kind": "text",
                        "text": "doktor"
                      }
                    ]
                  },
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "text": " ends in a consonant → "
                  },
                  {
                    "kind": "hilite",
                    "children": [
                      {
                        "kind": "text",
                        "text": "doktorduk"
                      }
                    ]
                  },
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "text": " (we were doctors)."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "kind": "paragraph",
            "text": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "text": "-(y)mIş takes "
              },
              {
                "kind": "strong",
                "children": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "text": "Group 2"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "text": " personal endings (the same set used with the -mIş perfect): -Im, -sIn, -(zero), -Iz, -sInIz, -lAr."
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "head": [
              "person",
              "stem + suffix",
              "meaning"
            ],
            "kind": "conjugation-table",
            "rows": [
              [
                "ben",
                "hasta-y-mış-ım",
                "I was apparently ill"
              ],
              [
                "sen",
                "hasta-y-mış-sın",
                "you were apparently ill"
              ],
              [
                "o",
                "hasta-y-mış",
                "he/she/it was apparently ill"
              ],
              [
                "biz",
