              }
            ]
          }
        ],
        "title": "examples in context"
      },
      {
        "id": "common-pitfalls",
        "body": [
          {
            "kind": "list",
            "items": [
              [
                {
                  "kind": "paragraph",
                  "text": [
                    {
                      "kind": "strong",
                      "children": [
                        {
                          "kind": "text",
                          "text": "Attaching the verbal -DI directly to a nominal."
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "kind": "text",
                      "text": " The verbal past suffix goes on verb stems only. On a nominal predicate you need the copula form with its buffer: "
                    },
                    {
                      "kind": "mono",
                      "children": [
                        {
                          "kind": "text",
                          "text": "✗ hastadım"
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "kind": "text",
                      "text": " → "
                    },
                    {
                      "kind": "mono",
                      "children": [
                        {
                          "kind": "text",
                          "text": "✓ hastaydım"
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "kind": "text",
                      "text": ". Without the -y- buffer the form is ungrammatical."
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ],
              [
                {
                  "kind": "paragraph",
                  "text": [
                    {
                      "kind": "strong",
                      "children": [
                        {
                          "kind": "text",
                          "text": "Using the wrong personal-ending group."
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "kind": "text",
                      "text": " -(y)DI takes Group 1 endings (-m, -n, -k, -nIz, -lAr), not Group 2. A common mistake is to add a Group 2 first-person ending: "
                    },
                    {
                      "kind": "mono",
                      "children": [
                        {
                          "kind": "text",
                          "text": "✗ hastaydıyım"
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "kind": "text",
                      "text": " → "
                    },
                    {
                      "kind": "mono",
                      "children": [
                        {
                          "kind": "text",
                          "text": "✓ hastaydım"
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "kind": "text",
                      "text": ". Reserve Group 2 endings for -(y)mIş."
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ],
              [
                {
                  "kind": "paragraph",
                  "text": [
                    {
                      "kind": "strong",
                      "children": [
                        {
                          "kind": "text",
                          "text": "Forgetting the -y- buffer after a vowel-final stem."
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "kind": "text",
                      "text": " Whenever the predicate ends in a vowel, the buffer consonant -y- is obligatory before both -(y)DI and -(y)mIş: "
                    },
                    {
                      "kind": "mono",
                      "children": [
                        {
                          "kind": "text",
                          "text": "✗ hastadı"
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "kind": "text",
                      "text": " → "
                    },
                    {
                      "kind": "mono",
                      "children": [
                        {
                          "kind": "text",
                          "text": "✓ hastaydı"
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "kind": "text",
                      "text": ". Consonant-final stems (e.g. "
                    },
                    {
                      "kind": "em",
                      "children": [
                        {
                          "kind": "text",
                          "text": "yorgun"
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "kind": "text",
                      "text": ") attach the suffix directly without a buffer."
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            ]
          }
        ],
        "title": "common pitfalls"
      }
    ],
    "subtitle": "-(y)DI and -(y)mIş on nouns, adjectives, and adverbials"
  }
}